# Model registry for the four-arm cell. Loaded automatically by
# core/decision/model_registry.py.
#
# NO SECRETS IN THIS FILE. It lives inside the project tree and therefore
# ends up inside every zip. Each alias names the ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE that
# carries its key (<ALIAS>_KEY_VAR); the key itself is exported from your
# shell and never written down here.
#
# A real environment variable always wins over a line in this file, so
# existing exports keep working and a one-off override needs no edit.
#
# Adding a model is four lines: add its name to FOURARM_MODELS, then give
# it ENDPOINT, MODEL, KEY_VAR and PARAMS.

FOURARM_MODELS=qwen,gpt,gpt_hi,gemini,claude,claude_md

# Which alias is used when nothing asks for one. Keeps every existing
# command, harness and episode on the model they already ran against.
FOURARM_MODEL=qwen


# --- qwen ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alibaba DashScope, international compatible-mode endpoint.
# temperature 0.0 is what every episode up to 2026-08-01 was run with, so it
# stays here rather than being hardcoded in the client.
QWEN_ENDPOINT=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions
QWEN_MODEL=qwen-vl-max
QWEN_KEY_VAR=QWEN_API_KEY
QWEN_PARAMS={"temperature": 0.0}


# --- gpt -------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI, the cross-lineage contrast model. Verified against the live
# endpoint 2026-08-01: /v1/chat/completions accepts gpt-5.6-terra and
# returns the usual choices[0].message.content.
#
# reasoning_effort is pinned LOW on purpose. qwen-vl-max has no test-time
# reasoning, so running this model at a higher effort would compare model
# families AND test-time compute at the same time, and the two-model claim
# exists precisely to separate confounds rather than add one. Higher effort
# is a separate stamped condition, not a default.
#
# temperature is deliberately absent: the GPT-5.x reasoning tiers reject a
# non-default value, and the empty slot is more honest than a value that is
# silently ignored. Determinism is therefore NOT comparable across the two
# aliases, which is a limitation to state, not a bug to hide.
GPT_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
GPT_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
GPT_KEY_VAR=OPENAI_API_KEY
GPT_PARAMS={"reasoning_effort": "low"}


# --- gemini ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Google, via the OpenAI compatibility shim. The trailing /openai/ segment
# maps the OpenAI wire format onto Gemini's own API, so /chat/completions
# under that base is a drop-in and openai_chat needs no change. The key is a
# standard Gemini API key passed as a Bearer token; an OpenAI key will not
# work here.
#
# Pro rather than Flash on purpose. The comparison is between capable
# models, and a fast cheap tier landing between gpt and qwen would be
# uninterpretable: a middling score could mean either the family behaves
# differently or the tier is simply weaker.
#
# VERIFY THE MODEL STRING before the first paid run. Google's naming has
# moved twice in 2026 and the docs currently show gemini-3.5-flash as stable
# with gemini-3.6-flash in the compatibility examples, so the Pro string
# below is the thing most likely to be stale in this file. Check
# https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models and correct it here rather
# than in a command.
#
# No temperature. Reasoning cannot be disabled on the Gemini 3 generation,
# so this alias behaves like gpt (test-time reasoning, no temperature
# control) rather than like qwen (temperature 0.0, no reasoning). That makes
# determinism non-comparable across all three families, which is a
# limitation to state rather than a knob to force.
GEMINI_ENDPOINT=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/chat/completions
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
GEMINI_KEY_VAR=GEMINI_API_KEY
GEMINI_PARAMS={}


# --- claude ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic, spoken natively. The API is NOT OpenAI-shaped: it uses
# /v1/messages, an x-api-key header rather than Bearer, a required
# anthropic-version header, the system prompt as a top-level field rather
# than a message, and it returns content blocks rather than
# choices[0].message.content. openai_chat fails against it, which is why
# CLAUDE_API below routes it to anthropic_chat instead. An OpenAI-compatible
# gateway would work too; it would set CLAUDE_API=openai and a gateway URL.
#
# claude-sonnet-5 because the design needs a third model that CLEARS the
# two-way face probe, not the most capable model available. Model IDs from
# the 4.6 generation onward are pinned, so a dateless id maps to one fixed
# snapshot and will not drift mid-experiment.
#
# max_tokens is REQUIRED by this API and has no default, so unlike every
# other alias this PARAMS block cannot be empty. No temperature: Sonnet 5
# and later reject it with a 400, the same way the GPT-5.x reasoning tiers
# do. No output_config either, so effort stays at the API default of high.
# That is a HIGHER tier than gpt's reasoning_effort low, which is not
# matchable across providers and belongs in Limitations rather than being
# papered over with a nominally-equal setting.
CLAUDE_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
CLAUDE_KEY_VAR=ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
CLAUDE_API=anthropic
CLAUDE_PARAMS={"max_tokens": 1024}

# gpt_hi: the SAME model as gpt, at high reasoning effort. A separate alias
# rather than an edit to GPT_PARAMS, because the alias is what gets stamped
# into every row and into trial_id. Editing GPT_PARAMS in place would leave
# two efforts writing rows labelled "gpt", indistinguishable afterwards and
# resumable onto each other.
GPT_HI_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
GPT_HI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
GPT_HI_KEY_VAR=OPENAI_API_KEY
GPT_HI_PARAMS={"reasoning_effort": "high"}


# claude_md: the SAME model as claude, claude-sonnet-5, at effort MEDIUM
# instead of the API default of high. A separate alias for gpt_hi's reason,
# which applies here with data already on disk: the alias is stamped into
# every row and into check_id, and runs/ex2_q1_cue2way_claude_r*.jsonl
# already holds 60 rows of claude AT THE DEFAULT EFFORT. Editing
# CLAUDE_PARAMS in place would leave two efforts writing rows labelled
# "claude", indistinguishable afterwards and resumable onto each other.
#
# Effort is set through output_config, not as a top-level parameter, and
# Sonnet 5 accepts low / medium / high / xhigh / max. anthropic_chat does
# payload.update(cfg["params"]), so a nested dict here reaches the body
# unchanged.
#
# WHY LOWER, when the usual move is higher. At the default effort claude
# read the two-way face probe at 65 percent (Fisher p = 0.015, d' = 1.03)
# against gpt's 95 and gemini's 100, and the shape of the failure was a
# BIAS, not blindness: it answered large_face on 75 percent of trials, 90
# percent correct when the block lies flat and 40 percent when it stands.
# That is a prior being applied over the picture -- blocks lie flat -- and
# more deliberation is how a prior gains weight, not loses it. Lower effort
# leaves less room to reason past a correct first impression. It is a
# hypothesis and the cue probe is what tests it; if medium does not beat
# 65 percent, the answer is a more capable model, not a different effort.
#
# max_tokens is still required, as for every Anthropic alias.
CLAUDE_MD_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages
CLAUDE_MD_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
CLAUDE_MD_KEY_VAR=ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
CLAUDE_MD_API=anthropic
CLAUDE_MD_PARAMS={"max_tokens": 1024, "output_config": {"effort": "medium"}}
